  "body": "Part of #894. Split out of #988 (whose PR covers the pass schedule, finish/spring passes, allowance and M4 cutters).\n\nWhat happens: the thread-milling ride reads each hole's (or boss's) own `entry_z` as the height its feeds start below; the operation's `top_z` (\"R plane (feed starts here)\" on the Heights tab) is shown but does not move where the feed starts.\n\nExpected: the stated R plane decides where the rapid stops and the feed begins (never below a feature's top, refused by name if it would rapid into stock), as on a drill cycle.\n\nDone means: the R plane is honoured for internal and external threads, pinned by a kernel test and a golden; defaults keep the #894/#985 goldens byte-identical. Safety floor: changes posted moves, so effort:high.\n",
